<TrustPage title="TriTimes Privacy" description="How TriTimes uses published race results, browser preferences, hosting, optional analytics, and its external feedback form." canonical="/privacy">
  <p>TriTimes displays publicly published triathlon results, including athlete names, countries, age groups, race placements, and split and finish times where available. Athlete histories bring together results associated with an athlete. This information comes from the results service described in the <a class="text-link" href="/faq">FAQ</a>. A public result can contain errors, and a combined history should not be treated as verified identity information.</p>
  <p>The site does not require an account to search athletes or view results. Search matching runs in your browser after downloading result indexes. Requests for search partitions, race data, and athlete data still reach the hosting provider. TriTimes uses your browser's local storage to remember an explicitly chosen light or dark theme and races you hide from an athlete view. You can remove those preferences by clearing this site's browser storage.</p>
  <p>Cloudflare serves the site and receives the network information needed to handle requests, such as IP addresses and requested URLs. When a Cloudflare Web Analytics token is configured for a build, the site also loads Cloudflare's analytics beacon. These services have their own data practices; see <a class="text-link" href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>. This page does not promise a retention period for provider logs.</p>
  <p>The feedback link leads to a Google-hosted form. Information you choose to submit is handled through that service, subject to <a class="text-link" href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a>. Avoid submitting sensitive personal information. For questions about a listing or a privacy concern, follow the instructions on the <a class="text-link" href="/contact">Contact page</a> and include the relevant TriTimes URL.</p>
</TrustPage>
